      "narrative": "Mara's eyes flick toward the bar, where Toran Vex sits with his back half-turned, one hand wrapped around a clay cup. She doesn't point, doesn't raise her voice\u2014just lets her gaze rest on him long enough for you to follow it.\n\n\"Toran Vex,\" she says, low and certain. \"Lockwright for the Kestrel Guild. He's the one who kept the Ash Gate's mechanism working all these years. Filed the tumblers, oiled the bolts, made sure the seal held proper.\"\n\nShe takes a sip from her mug, watching you over the rim.\n\n\"He's not talking about it, though. Not to me, not to anyone. Every time the Gate comes up, he finds a reason to be somewhere else.\" She sets the mug down. \"But you're asking the right questions. If there's a crack in that silence, it's gonna take more than a friendly nudge to open it.\"\n\nShe gestures with her chin toward Toran.\n\n\"Your move. What do you want to do about him?\""
    },
