      "narrative": "Mara's fingers tighten around her mug. She holds your gaze for a long breath, then sets the cup down with a soft clack.\n\n\"His name's Sable Quill.\" She says it plainly, but there's an edge beneath it. \"Courier for the Kestrel Guild. Travel-stained cloak, always moving, always quiet. He's the one who took the coin and opened the Gate for those who couldn't wait.\"\n\nShe leans forward, voice dropping to a murmur.\n\n\"Bram knew. That's what I think, anyway. Sable would row people across after dusk\u2014Guild merchants, a few desperate souls with heavy purses. Off the books, under the seal of silence. And Bram...\" She trails off, glancing toward the shuttered window that faces the Gate's direction. \"Bram was found dead the morning after one of those crossings. No marks. No blood. Just gone.\"\n\nShe meets your eyes again.\n\n\"Sable Quill's still around. I saw him at the Gate landing two mornings ago, pretending to check a strap on his satchel. He's waiting for something\u2014or someone.\"\n\nShe lets the silence settle, then adds, softer:\n\n\"You want the truth about that Gate? Sable Quill's the one who sold passage through it. And he might be the one who knows why Bram ended up cold on that landing.\""
    },
