      "narrative": "Your voice cuts through the damp air, carrying across the platform.\n\n\"Bram! Old Bram!\"\n\nThe name echoes off the arch, swallowed by the mist. For a moment, nothing. Just the distant churn of water below, the creak of the dock's mooring post.\n\nThen the figure in the travel-stained cloak turns.\n\nHe's lean, sharp-featured, with the hollowed look of someone who hasn't slept well in days. His eyes lock onto you\u2014not startled, not angry. Watchful. He takes a slow step back from the arch's edge, hand resting on his satchel strap.\n\n\"Bram's not here,\" he says. Voice flat, careful. \"He's dead. Eight days now.\"\n\nHe studies you a moment longer.\n\n\"You a friend of his? Or just passing through?\""
