      "narrative": "You drop to a crouch beneath the arch, fingers brushing the damp flagstones. The surface looks uniform at first\u2014grey stone, dark with moisture, scattered grit\u2014but your touch catches something. A faint seam, almost invisible against the weathered rock. You press, and a section of stone shifts with a dry scrape.\n\nA small compartment, cleverly fitted into the base of the arch.\n\nInside: two vials, side by side, each filled with a liquid that glows a soft, steady blue\u2014like captured starlight diluted in water. The glass is cool to the touch. And the dust around them... it's disturbed. Not the settled layer of weeks, but the uneven scatter of hours. Someone placed these here recently.\n\nSable Quill's boots scrape on the stone behind you. He hasn't moved closer, but his voice comes sharp and low.\n\n\"What did you find?\""
