      "narrative": "The Copper Finch's door groans open, and the warmth of the common room washes over you\u2014smoke, ale, damp wool. The same few travellers nurse cups by the window. The same fire crackles low in the hearth.\n\nYour old table stands empty. The one near the back wall, scarred wood, a view of the room.\n\nYou sit.\n\nA moment passes. Then footsteps. Mara Venn appears at your table's edge, a fresh mug in each hand. She sets one down in front of you\u2014steaming, dark, bitter-smelling\u2014and slides into the seat across.\n\nHer eyes trace your face, reading what they find there.\n\n\"You went to the Gate,\" she says. Not a question. \"And you came back. That's more than some can say.\" She wraps her hands around her own mug, watching you. \"So. Did you find what you were looking for?\""
